{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q223197","formula":"Al₂Si₂O₅(OH)₄","hill":"Al2H4O9Si2","elements":["H","O","Al","Si"],"composition":{"H":4.0,"O":9.0,"Al":2.0,"Si":2.0},"names":{"en":"Kaolinite","ru":"Каолинит","uk":"Каолініт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Kaolinite ( KAY-ə-lə-nyte, -⁠lih-; also called kaolin) is a clay mineral, having the chemical composition Al2Si2O5(OH)4. It is a layered silicate mineral, with one \"tetrahedral\" sheet of silicate tetrahedra (SiO4) linked to one \"octahedral\" sheet of aluminate octahedrons (AlO2(OH)4) through oxygen atoms on one side, and another such sheet linked through hydrogen bonds on the other side. Kaolinite is a soft, earthy, usually white, mineral (dioctahedral phyllosilicate clay), produced by the chemical weathering of aluminium silicate minerals like feldspar.","ru":"Каолини́т (от Каолин) — глинистый минерал из группы водных силикатов алюминия.","uk":"Каоліні́т — мінерал класу силікатів, основний силікат алюмінію шаруватої будови. Назва перейшла від китайського «кау-лінг» — висока гора (так називалося родовище каолінів)."},"fame":66,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-541152","atoms":34,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[5.213,0.0,0.0],[1.932,7.225,0.0],[0.043,0.281,9.047]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":2.944,"y":4.06,"z":4.46,"el":"Al"},{"x":2.936,"y":4.147,"z":7.498,"el":"Al"},{"x":5.584,"y":4.178,"z":8.98,"el":"Al"},{"x":5.51,"y":4.034,"z":2.973,"el":"Al"},{"x":2.115,"y":6.798,"z":3.051,"el":"Si"},{"x":2.192,"y":6.867,"z":6.024,"el":"Si"},{"x":4.733,"y":6.92,"z":7.578,"el":"Si"},{"x":4.787,"y":6.735,"z":1.5,"el":"Si"},{"x":2.404,"y":5.002,"z":0.547,"el":"H"},{"x":1.192,"y":2.129,"z":1.552,"el":"H"},{"x":1.112,"y":2.256,"z":4.558,"el":"H"},{"x":1.171,"